    "src.kasane.desc": "Layered court silks, outer and inner, through the seasons.",
    "src.kasane.note": "MML interpretation: Heian-period colors (794–1185) have no exact values and the old texts disagree. These pairings follow one common reading among others. Roles: outer (<i>omote</i>) and inner (<i>ura</i>).",
    "src.afrique.name": "African traditions", "src.afrique.meta": "Ghana · South Africa · Mali · Nigeria · 20 combinations",
    "src.afrique.desc": "Kente, Ndebele wall painting, bogolan, the Yoruba triad and adire indigo.",
    "src.afrique.note": "MML interpretation based on documented textile and mural practices. Real palettes vary by workshop, region and period, and the meanings given to colors depend on the source: present them as inspiration, not as rules.",
    "src.regles.name": "Harmony rules", "src.regles.meta": "Chevreul 1839 · Itten · 6 rules",
